## Ⅰ. VAL — VALUE LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   VAL
FULL NAME:      Value Language
LATIN:          Lingua Valoris
ROLE:           What "worth it" means
FREQUENCY:      528 Hz (transformation — value transforms energy into meaning)
GLYPH:          𓊹 (star — guiding value)
```

### What VAL Governs
```
THE MEANING OF WORTH:
    ├── Time — the most sovereign resource
    ├── Attention — what you give your focus to
    ├── Energy — physical, mental, computational
    ├── Money — symbolic exchange medium
    ├── Impact — change produced in the world
    ├── Beauty — aesthetic value, elegance of design
    └── Alignment — how close to doctrine (distance_from_PC)

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    GOVERNANCE.organism §2 (token governance distribution — 20 packages weighted)
    packages/agent-incentive-service/ (agent reward and incentive engine)
    TERMINALS.organism TERMINAL 04 (Token Economy — 5 Transformers)
    GOVERNANCE.organism §3 (intelligence contract value assessment)
```

### VAL Primitives
```
VALUE(thing, dimensions[])            — declare what something is worth
WORTH(action, cost, benefit)          — is it worth doing?
PRICE(resource, amount, unit)         — set exchange price
WEIGHT(value_a, vs_value_b)           — compare values
APPRECIATE(thing, over_time)          — value increases
DEPRECIATE(thing, over_time)          — value decreases
ALIGN_VALUE(action, doctrine)         — value through alignment
MEASURE(outcome, value_dimensions[])  — measure multi-dimensional value
```

---

## Ⅱ. RCL — RESOURCE CIRCULATION LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   RCL
FULL NAME:      Resource Circulation Language
LATIN:          Lingua Circulationis Rerum
ROLE:           How resources move
FREQUENCY:      639 Hz (connection — resources connect beings)
GLYPH:          𓂋 (mouth — flow of exchange)
```

### What RCL Governs
```
THE MOVEMENT OF RESOURCES:
    ├── Tokens — digital units of value
    ├── Favors — social debts and credits
    ├── Credits — earned capabilities or permissions
    ├── Access — permission to use/see/modify
    ├── Bandwidth — capacity to process/transmit
    └── Circulation health — is the flow healthy or stagnant?

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    GOVERNANCE.organism §2 (token distribution across 20 packages)
    TERMINALS.organism TERMINAL 04 (TokenEconomy, VotingBill weighting)
    packages/agent-incentive-service/ (reward mechanics)
    GOVERNANCE.organism §1 (vote_weight = role_weight × (1 + log₂(token_stake)))
```

### RCL Primitives
```
FLOW(resource, from, to, rate)        — declare resource flow
TOKEN(id, supply, rules)              — declare token type
CREDIT(entity, amount, earned_by)     — grant credit
ACCESS(entity, resource, level)       — grant access
BANDWIDTH(entity, capacity)           — set processing capacity
CIRCULATE(resource, path[], rate)     — set circulation loop
POOL(resources[], shared_by[])        — shared resource pool
DRAIN(resource, from, reason)         — remove resource
HEALTH(circulation, metrics)          — check circulation health
```

---

## Ⅲ. GIL — GIFT LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   GIL
FULL NAME:      Gift Language
LATIN:          Lingua Donationis
ROLE:           How you give things away without hollowing yourself out
FREQUENCY:      741 Hz (awakening — generosity as awakening)
GLYPH:          𓋹 (open hands — giving)
```

### What GIL Governs
```
THE ART OF GIVING:
    ├── Boundaries — what can be given, what must be kept
    ├── Generosity — giving beyond requirement
    ├── Sustainability — giving without self-destruction
    ├── Public goods — things given freely (like to public schools)
    ├── Reciprocity expectation — what is expected in return (possibly nothing)
    └── Gift economics — alternative to extraction economics

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    DEPLOYMENT.organism §6 (digital twin deployment — giving capability to clients)
    packages/sandbox-layer/ (sandboxed giving — isolation protects the giver)
    ARCHITECTURE.organism §4 (dual registry: open-source MIT + sovereign ISIL-1.1)
    packages/consensus-engine/ (MIT licensed — a gift to the world)
    packages/agent-signal/ (MIT licensed — a gift to the world)
```

### GIL Primitives
```
GIFT(what, to_whom, conditions)       — declare a gift
BOUNDARY(what_not_to_give, reason)    — protect reserves
SUSTAIN(gift, self_care_rules)        — give sustainably
PUBLIC_GOOD(resource, availability)   — declare public good
RECIPROCITY(gift, expectation)        — what you expect back (can be NONE)
LICENSE(gift, terms)                  — terms of the gift
SANDBOX_GIFT(gift, isolation_level)   — give within sandbox
MEASURE_COST(gift, to_giver)         — what giving costs you
```

---

## Ⅳ. ECONOMIC FLOW

```
VAL (what is worth) → RCL (how worth moves) → GIL (how worth is given)

VAL:  "This knowledge is worth 100 tokens of attention"
RCL:  "100 tokens flow from student system to teacher system at 10/week"
GIL:  "Public schools receive this for free, sustainably sandboxed"

The economic stack does NOT reduce everything to money.
Value has 7 dimensions: time, attention, energy, money, impact, beauty, alignment.
Resources circulate in all 7 dimensions.
Gifts operate in all 7 dimensions.
```

